    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIaAtr">VIIa Atr</ref> 2.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-d">⁊ sceote man æghwilce hide pænig oððe pæniges weorð.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.2" corresp="#wit-d">⁊ sceote man æghwilce hide pænige oððe pæniges weorð.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And from every hide a penny or the value of a penny shall be given as dues.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">And one penny or the value of one penny is to be paid from each hide.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und man steuere [von] jeder Hufe einen Pfennig oder Pfennigs Werth.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let a penny or a penny's worth be paid [from] every hide.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Napier corrects to ‘æt æghwilcre’. Liebermann compares VII Atr 1.2.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">id. has carruca “plough”, instead of hide</note>
      </div>
    </body>
